 or not have a few tests  around see which ones you like which  ones you don't like and then pick one or  two if you had some artifacts combine  them with the color that you've picked  next you need to separate cards  depending on their mana very that's the  number of symbols on the top right of  the card cards that aren't artifacts  will usually have a number and then two  symbols you add these all together so  the war chanter of Mogis has three and  then two skulls that means it's a five  you'll then come across things called  basic lands ru swamps because I'm a  black player separate these as well  lenz are very important so the way the  nervous system  cards works is that if a card has three  and a skull for example it's worth four  swamps you need to have four swamps on  the field to actually be able to summon  that card so the reason that you  separated your cards into numbers is  because obviously as you start playing  you will have a limited amount of swamps  meaning the cards you can summon will be  available matter value I guard for  example is worth one skull which means  that I would be able to play that on the  very first turn of any game much miss  title is a seven sometimes I may not  ever be able to get to a seven a game  could be over before that so the idea  here is that you want to have more ones  in your cards than sevens you also want  to have a deck of roughly 60 cards so  what I would normally do here is go  through the highest number and decide  which cards I really really want to keep  and get rid of everything that I don't  really really want as I get close to the  one I'll be more lenient and allow  myself to have more cards with the low  amount of value you can only have four  copies of any one card in your deck at  any one time  once you've separated all your cards  into piles and you've gotten rid of all  the cards you don't care about pick up  your cards and count how many you have  left over I ended up with twenty cards  and like I said before morester should  be about sixty because I only had twenty  I'm only going to add thirty lands what  I'm left with is a black deck with fifty  cards with mostly man on one cost but I  still have some sevens in there in case  the manor gets that by now this is the  most simple way to make a deck there are  far more complicated ways you can do it  this is probably just the best way for a  beginner to figure out that deck and  start playing the cards and figuring out  what they like and what they don't like  so hopefully that helps some of you out  I'm not sure if it's the right way to do  it but it's the way that echo is done it  and when you have more cards it works a  lot better but I tend to win a lot of  game so I feel like I'm doing something  right but now I have a holiday pack and  two throws intro packs to give you guys  unfortunately this one's only open to  Australian residents because shipping is  kind of expensive but for your chance to  win I want you to tell me what color you  do play as or what color you would play  as if you started playing magic  gathering and why the most  heads will win and competition will  close a week after I've posted this I'll  send the winners a message on YouTube so  hopefully you guys check your inboxes so  I can get your address and send you out  some grease I'll see you guys next time  bye
 

